From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Srirangan Madhavan <smadhavan@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 01:02:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: cxl: Split decoder programming into a
 reusable helper

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2163076

Move common HDM decoder settings to include/cxl/cxl.h and route the
register programming sequence through cxl_commit(). This lets reset code
restore cached HDM state without depending on private cxl_core types while
keeping hdm.c in charge of the existing commit policy checks.

Build the low-level HDM helper under CONFIG_CXL_HDM so it is available even
when cxl_core is modular.

Signed-off-by: Srirangan Madhavan <smadhavan@nvidia.com>
(backported from https://lore.kernel.org/linux-cxl/20260709010304.680422-1-smadhavan@nvidia.com/)
[jan: keep pre-existing <linux/pci.h> alongside the added <linux/range.h> in
include/cxl/cxl.h, and drop the tools/testing/cxl/test/cxl.c hunks since the
cxl_test decoder-registry helper they touch is not present in NV-Kernels 7.0-bos]
Signed-off-by: Jiandi An <jan@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Seth Forshee <sforshee@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Matthew R. Ochs <mochs@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-01870
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@2f00a17240629e30bc2de37feef32cc2124fd75e
